"version":1,"versionNonce":662710749,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Deployed - passive-fire-roan.vercel.app on\nSupabase cloud; gated GitHub Actions deploy not\nyet enabled","originalText":"Deployed - passive-fire-roan.vercel.app on\nSupabase cloud; gated GitHub Actions deploy not\nyet enabled","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"text","id":"te660","x":0,"y":-1028.6,"width":2344.3199999999997,"height":27.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#b91c1c","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":2041867934,"version":1,"versionNonce":1953935571,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Next human steps: enable the gated CI deploy (Vercel token + DEPLOY_ENABLED), write the agentic-coding account, then Stage 6 non-functional tickets.","originalText":"Next human steps: enable the gated CI deploy (Vercel token + DEPLOY_ENABLED), write the agentic-coding account, then Stage 6 non-functional tickets.","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"text","id":"te661","x":0,"y":-958.5999999999999,"width":1425.6,"height":37.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#2563eb","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":1569384936,"version":1,"versionNonce":843735105,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"My understanding of the assignment, and what this submission shows","originalText":"My understanding of the assignment, and what this submission shows","fontSize":30,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"rectangle","id":"re662","x":0,"y":-898.5999999999999,"width":1036,"height":230,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#f59e0b","backgroundColor":"#fff3bf","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":80725503,"version":1,"versionNonce":41212477,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},{"type":"text","id":"te663","x":16,"y":-884.5999999999999,"width":491.03999999999996,"height":27.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":2111425230,"version":1,"versionNonce":1870797563,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Understanding of the assignment","originalText":"Understanding of the assignment","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"text","id":"te664","x":16,"y":-844.5999999999999,"width":1308.96,"height":90.0,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1f2937","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":1512432847,"version":1,"versionNonce":374133116,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Use a software engineering methodology to convert a business requirement into a technical solution.\nThis submission shows that conversion step by step: problem summary -> use cases -> context and scope\n-> business process -> data flow -> domain model -> database ER -> interactions -> delivery tickets\n-> working slice.","originalText":"Use a software engineering methodology to convert a business requirement into a technical solution.\nThis submission shows that conversion step by step: problem summary -> use cases -> context and scope\n-> business process -> data flow -> domain model -> database ER -> interactions -> delivery tickets\n-> working slice.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"rectangle","id":"re665","x":1060,"y":-898.5999999999999,"width":1036,"height":230,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#4a9eed","backgroundColor":"#a5d8ff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":16041722,"version":1,"versionNonce":1527209466,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},{"type":"text","id":"te666","x":1076,"y":-884.5999999999999,"width":902.88,"height":27.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":1479865565,"version":1,"versionNonce":1987205178,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"How I used AI agents (only part of the approach is shown)","originalText":"How I used AI agents (only part of the approach is shown)","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"text","id":"te667","x":1076,"y":-844.5999999999999,"width":1296.0,"height":112.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1f2937","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":1394201352,"version":1,"versionNonce":1318928523,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Repo guideline for agents: CLAUDE.md, .mcp.json and skills. A GLOSSARY.md so people and agents share\none domain language. Plan before execution, and spec-driven development (iteration plan, slice spec,\ntechnical design, test strategy). An agent iteration guideline: one issue = one branch = one PR,\ntests first, quality gates, self diff review, human review gate. MCP used for the browser\n(Playwright), database (Supabase) and deployment (Vercel).","originalText":"Repo guideline for agents: CLAUDE.md, .mcp.json and skills. A GLOSSARY.md so people and agents share\none domain language. Plan before execution, and spec-driven development (iteration plan, slice spec,\ntechnical design, test strategy). An agent iteration guideline: one issue = one branch = one PR,\ntests first, quality gates, self diff review, human review gate. MCP used for the browser\n(Playwright), database (Supabase) and deployment (Vercel).","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"rectangle","id":"re668","x":0,"y":-638.5999999999999,"width":1036,"height":348,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#ef4444","backgroundColor":"#ffc9c9","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":1107025864,"version":1,"versionNonce":979489499,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},{"type":"text","id":"te669","x":16,"y":-624.5999999999999,"width":522.72,"height":27.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":1834003415,"version":1,"versionNonce":2027127194,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Not covered in the implementation","originalText":"Not covered in the implementation","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"text","id":"te670","x":16,"y":-584.5999999999999,"width":1308.96,"height":247.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1f2937","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":626908888,"version":1,"versionNonce":1333651108,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"- Dedicated UX/UI design work (the screens are functional, not designed).\n- Most non-functional requirements beyond the basics: observability, real authentication, rate\n  limiting and throttling, BFF / proxy, scalability and a full content security policy - see the\n  Stage 6 tickets.\n- A resolution does not change readiness yet. Resolving as stock arriving, a different solution\n  nominated or rescheduled only records the decision: no delivery, nomination or new date is created,\n  so the planned work stays Short and the team leader is not shown the resolution on it. Next: show\n  the resolution on the planned work (A); later let resolutions record the delivery, the approved\n  nomination or the new date so readiness recalculates (B, iteration 2).\n- No live updates: an open page does not refresh itself when someone else changes the data (would\n  need Supabase Realtime or polling).","originalText":"- Dedicated UX/UI design work (the screens are functional, not designed).\n- Most non-functional requirements beyond the basics: observability, real authentication, rate\n  limiting and throttling, BFF / proxy, scalability and a full content security policy - see the\n  Stage 6 tickets.\n- A resolution does not change readiness yet. Resolving as stock arriving, a different solution\n  nominated or rescheduled only records the decision: no delivery, nomination or new date is created,\n  so the planned work stays Short and the team leader is not shown the resolution on it. Next: show\n  the resolution on the planned work (A); later let resolutions record the delivery, the approved\n  nomination or the new date so readiness recalculates (B, iteration 2).\n- No live updates: an open page does not refresh itself when someone else changes the data (would\n  need Supabase Realtime or polling).","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"rectangle","id":"re671","x":1060,"y":-638.5999999999999,"width":1036,"height":348,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#757575","backgroundColor":"#e9ecef","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":635066309,"version":1,"versionNonce":1710251482,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},{"type":"text","id":"te672","x":1076,"y":-624.5999999999999,"width":443.52,"height":27.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":225201199,"version":1,"versionNonce":1922537217,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Assumptions about boundaries","originalText":"Assumptions about boundaries","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"text","id":"te673","x":1076,"y":-584.5999999999999,"width":1283.04,"height":67.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1f2937","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":962507851,"version":1,"versionNonce":90825396,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"The boundaries between QAntum platform, supplier catalogue, stock and this new capability are based\non my reading of the brief and the supplied solutions CSV. They may not match the real platform;\nproducts, quantities, stock and schedules are SAMPLE data.","originalText":"The boundaries between QAntum platform, supplier catalogue, stock and this new capability are based\non my reading of the brief and the supplied solutions CSV. They may not match the real platform;\nproducts, quantities, stock and schedules are SAMPLE data.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"rectangle","id":"re674","x":0,"y":-260.5999999999999,"width":2096,"height":132,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#15803d","backgroundColor":"#b2f2bb","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":1355907829,"version":1,"versionNonce":1724496007,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},{"type":"text","id":"te675","x":16,"y":-246.5999999999999,"width":570.24,"height":27.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":254447169,"version":1,"versionNonce":1942505832,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"What the implementation demonstrates","originalText":"What the implementation demonstrates","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true},{"type":"text","id":"te676","x":16,"y":-206.5999999999999,"width":2630.88,"height":45.0,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1f2937","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":837889819,"version":1,"versionNonce":236698106,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"One simple, end-to-end workflow: a team leader checks whether the planned work for the next 14 days is Ready, Short or Unknown against stock and expected deliveries, and escalates a shortage to a project\nmanager, who resolves it (stock arriving, a different solution nominated, or rescheduled) - working offline-first on mobile and desktop.","originalText":"One simple, end-to-end workflow: a team leader checks whether the planned work for the next 14 days is Ready, Short or Unknown against stock and expected deliveries, and escalates a shortage to a project\nmanager, who resolves it (stock arriving, a different solution nominated, or rescheduled) - working offline-first on mobile and desktop.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":true}],"appState":{"viewBackgroundColor":"#ffffff","gridSize":null},"files":{"b5d8a17a47c74a7a4aa78bda533b82bc184e8f1b":{"mimeType":"image/jpeg","id":"b5d8a17a47c74a7a4aa78bda533b82bc184e8f1b","created":1,"dataURL":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"1ff1b1e3eb7f36db5b6c431d4681338488418ddf":{"mimeType":"image/jpeg","id":"1ff1b1e3eb7f36db5b6c431d4681338488418ddf","created":1,"dataURL":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"99dd362a73533979491b9501857b117982aad776":{"mimeType":"image/jpeg","id":"99dd362a73533979491b9501857b117982aad776","created":1,"dataURL":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"7ef024d767d6941cb90bbcd9d42df4b0aee4719d":{"mimeType":"image/jpeg","id":"7ef024d767d6941cb90bbcd9d42df4b0aee4719d","created":1,"dataURL":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"809f92da2431aa22f853e4349a72ad1d245432a8":{"mimeType":"image/jpeg","id":"809f92da2431aa22f853e4349a72ad1d245432a8","created":1,"dataURL":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"dc64bbb32784617092f3f596d29c6a84da78bcc4":{"mimeType":"image/jpeg","id":"dc64bbb32784617092f3f596d29c6a84da78bcc4","created":1,"dataURL":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"9a81a23bebb80762a604bfbfd60b7730d4d4ad6d":{"mimeType":"image/jpeg","id":"9a81a23bebb80762a604bfbfd60b7730d4d4ad6d","created":1,"dataURL":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"13541b09b9e3745f9742